And what exactly do you need it for? Nethack isn't a adventure game in 
the original sense where you need to keep complete maps. Once 
discovered the maps stay in place when you enter a level again. Only 
certain events trigger loss of memory (and thus maps) and they are 
rather easily avoided. Also, even if you loose parts of a map to let's 
say a scroll of amnesia or a mind flayer it will still be as empty of 
monsters as when you left it (if you usually kill everything in sight 
:-). So remapping a few levels is not that tedious. Once you get lower 
down you really *should* take care not to get hit by amnesia.


